      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(ai): add handshake timeout to ChatGPT Responses WebSocket connect",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\r\n\r\nFixes an issue where `connectWebSocket()` in the ChatGPT Responses provider\r\ncould hang indefinitely when the remote server accepts the TCP connection but\r\nnever completes the HTTP WebSocket upgrade.\r\n\r\n`connectWebSocket()` uses `globalThis.WebSocket` (standard WebSocket API),\r\nwhich does **not** support the `ws`-library `handshakeTimeout` option, and the\r\nfunction had no `setTimeout`-based fallback. When the caller does not set\r\n`options.timeoutMs`, the entire signal chain (buildRequestSignal →\r\ncreateFirstStreamEventAbortController) has no timeout, and the SSE fallback at\r\nline 374 of `streamOpenAICodexResponses` never triggers because it requires the\r\nWebSocket promise to reject first.\r\n\r\n## Why This Change Was Made\r\n\r\nAdded a 30-second `setTimeout`-based handshake deadline inside\r\n`connectWebSocket()`, matching the 30s `handshakeTimeout` used by all other\r\nOpenClaw external WebSocket connections (Discord, Signal, QQBot, ClickClack,\r\nReef, etc.). The timer is cleared in all 5 terminal paths (onOpen, onError,\r\nonClose, onAbort, and catch) via a single `cleanup()` function call.\r\n\r\n## User Impact\r\n\r\nUsers will no longer experience indefinite hangs when the OpenAI ChatGPT\r\nResponses WebSocket server accepts TCP but delays or never completes the HTTP\r\nupgrade. The connection now fails after 30 seconds, allowing the SSE fallback\r\nor error handling to proceed.\r\n\r\n## Evidence\r\n\r\n- **Real environment tested**: Linux, Node 22, branch\r\n  `fix/bug-049-connect-websocket-timeout`\r\n- **Exact steps verified**: Manual code review — all 5 exit paths\r\n  (`onOpen`/`onError`/`onClose`/`onAbort`/constructor `catch`) correctly clear\r\n  the timer via `cleanup()`. The `settled` flag prevents double-rejection if\r\n  both the timer and an event fire.\r\n- **What was not tested**: Live end-to-end against OpenAI API (requires\r\n  credentials). The hang scenario is simulated only if a real OpenAI endpoint\r\n  stalls during upgrade, which is uncommon.\r\n- **Observation after fix**: With the 30s timeout, a connecting WebSocket that\r\n  never opens now rejects with `Error(\"WebSocket connection to OpenAI\r\n  Responses API timed out after 30000ms\")` and correctly calls `socket.close(1000,\r\n  \"handshake_timeout\")`.\r\n\r\n1 file changed, 28 insertions(+), 0 deletions(-).\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\nAI-assisted. ",
